# `-1e400` must be refused too. The lexer never sees the sign: unary minus is its
# own token, so the magnitude `1e400` hits the range check on its own and the
# message quotes it without the sign. That is why this is a separate fixture --
# the negated form travels a different route (const_fold's unary-minus arm would
# have negated the infinity) and asserting it costs three lines.
#
# Flat file, no `package` header -- see the note above this lane in tests/run.sh.
# The exact wording lives in tests/diag/float_lit_overflow.ty; this lane asserts
# only that the compiler refuses and says something.
fn main():
    x := -1e400
    println(str(x))
